</pre></div><h2 class="h2">Plotting Time Series Data for a Single Subject</h2><p>Given that the Human Activity Recognition (HAR) dataset has time series as data, it’s necessary to review the raw signals. This confirms the quality of the data and finds regularities associated with different physical exercises.</p><p>A data sample has 50% of its sensor readings repeated by taken from the previous sample, so care must be taken to remove these repeated points.</p><h3 class="h3">Step 1: Load Training Data</h3><p>A helper function called load_dataset() is used to load all the data in the training set.</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">trainX, trainy = load_dataset('train', 'HARDataset/') 
</textarea></div><h3 class="h3">Step 2: After the airframe has been loaded, load your subject mapping.</h3><p>The dataset has each subject in a different row. The file is loaded with load_file(), and unique subjects are taken out.</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="xml" name="code">sub_map = load_file('HARDataset/train/subject_train.txt')
